Modifications for MDViewer (2026): ported the frontend to a Tauri desktop
application with Next.js static export; removed analytics, website SEO and
remote font loading; added a read-only document shell and default-open table
of contents; restored local block editing and hash-checked saving.

The HWP import and HWPX export code is derived from the original MDView
hwp-parser.worker.ts and hwp-generator.worker.ts (Apache-2.0). For MDViewer's
third stage, this code was separated into pure parser/generator modules and
Web Workers. The HWPX parser was rewritten with namespace-aware XML traversal,
and the generator was rewritten to produce an OCF HWPX package. HWP picture
record/BinData ID mapping was corrected. Added explicit conversion warnings,
resource limits, read-only import, and transactional first-save image assets.
Table/picture caption text is retained with text-only layout warnings; field
metadata reductions preserve display text and report explicit body markers.
No original HWP/HWPX document is modified by import.

Read-only original document rendering includes @rhwp/core 0.8.7:
https://github.com/edwardkim/rhwp
https://www.npmjs.com/package/@rhwp/core/v/0.8.7
The unmodified rhwp_bg.wasm is bundled locally. No Hancom fonts are bundled.

